  "lines": [
   {
    "t0": 0.07,
    "t1": 4.18,
    "text": "Don't use C code unless you've installed these five plugins The first is Omniro,",
    "rate": 3.4
   },
   {
    "t0": 4.18,
    "t1": 16.7,
    "text": "which gives Clacode almost unlimited usage by connecting to over 200 free AI API providers so the moment your usage limit runs out it will automatically switch you to the next best model getting up to 1.6 billion free tokens every single month.",
    "rate": 3.5
   },
   {
    "t0": 16.87,
    "t1": 40.66,
    "text": "The second is Cla Mem it gives cloud memory across every session so it'll start remembering projects and files that you ever having to reexplain a single thing The third is called headroom This sits between you and your AI model and only passes through the parts that actually matter compressing and removing all the unnecessary stuff so you guys will get the same results with way fewer tokens the fourth is Cla code setup which is an official anthropic plugin that scans your entire code base and actually recommends the best hooks,",
    "rate": 3.9
   },
   {
    "t0": 40.66,
    "t1": 40.97,
    "text": "skills,",
    "rate": 3.2
   },
   {
    "t0": 40.97,
    "t1": 48.19,
    "text": "subagents and even MCP servers to fit your project and it'll remove all of the unnecessary and useless fluff and finally task observer they'll watch how you work.",
    "rate": 3.9
   },
   {
    "t0": 48.26,
    "t1": 52.71,
    "text": "Learn your style and constantly improve your other skills in the background for you entirely automatically,",
    "rate": 3.6
   },
   {
    "t0": 52.71,
    "t1": 57.28,
    "text": "so if you guys want to try this for yourself, just comment Cla down below and I'll send you the link directly.",
    "rate": 4.8
   }
  ]
 },
